# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUG-563 / D-2684 (2026-09-27): THIS FILE IS A DECLARATION, NOT A CONVENIENCE LIST.
# MEASURED before this: 124 dirty paths and 112 of them `backups/**` - PRE-IMAGES that C13/R-D410 OBLIGE a
# session to write and that no plan may commit. So the tree could never be clean and the evidence trail was
# unversioned BY ACCIDENT rather than by decision. A path is now either INDEXED (granted, named, in
# governance/session_plan_20260924.yaml#may_touch) or DECLARED EXCLUDED - and the two homes are ONE fact with
# ONE reader: scripts/check_repo_integrity.py --worktree, whose declarations and reasons live in
# config/repo_integrity.yaml#worktree.excluded. An exclusion declared there but NOT honoured here is a FAULT
# (the rail asks git itself: `git check-ignore --no-index`), so this block cannot drift from that one.
# NOTE: an ignore rule does NOT untrack a tracked path. The three tracked owner revisions under backups/ and
# the historical drift_report_*/bench_preflight_* snapshots stay in history and stay tracked.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
backups/
governance/drift_report_2*.json
governance/bench_preflight_2*.json
# D-2800 (BUG-563 recurrence, 2026-10-03): ephemeral runtime lock + owner source material.
# Declared in config/repo_integrity.yaml#worktree.excluded (each with a why); these bytes are the EXCLUSION.
.pipeline_runner.lock
governance/*.numbers
governance/anchor ruler*.csv

# Transient run logs (results JSONs are the durable artifact; logs stay on disk, unversioned)
logs/
*.log
